# Privacy Policy — Salat

**Last updated: 23 June 2026**

This Privacy Policy explains how the **Salat** app ("Salat", "the app", "we", "us")
handles information when you use it. Salat is an Islamic prayer-times app for
Android.

**Summary:** Salat has **no servers of its own** and does **not require an account**.
We do not collect or store your personal data. Prayer-time and Qibla calculations
happen **on your device**. The only data leaving your device is anonymous usage
analytics and advertising data handled by Google (Firebase Analytics and Google
AdMob), as described below.

---

## 1. Information we process

### a) Location
Salat uses your device location (or a city you enter manually) **only on your
device** to calculate prayer times and the Qibla (direction to the Kaaba). To
display your city name, your device's operating system may convert your
coordinates into a place name using its built-in geocoding service.

We do **not** store your location and we do **not** send it to any server operated
by us (we operate none). Your location is cached locally on your device so the app
works offline.

You can deny or revoke the location permission at any time in your device settings
and instead select a city manually.

### b) Usage and analytics (Google Firebase Analytics)
To understand how the app is used and improve reliability and retention, Salat uses
**Google Firebase Analytics**, which collects **anonymous** usage and diagnostic
information such as app opens, session data, device model, operating-system
version, language/region, and in-app events (for example: onboarding completed,
notification permission granted, calculation method changed). This data does not
identify you personally and we do not combine it with any personal information.

### c) Advertising (Google AdMob)
Salat shows ads through **Google AdMob** to keep the app free. To serve ads, Google
may use device and advertising identifiers (such as the Advertising ID) and related
information. Where required (for example in the European Economic Area and the UK),
the app asks for your consent through Google's consent form before serving
personalized ads; you may choose non-personalized ads.

### d) Notifications and on-device settings
Your preferences (calculation method, madhab, manual adjustments, chosen language,
adhan modes, Hijri offset) are stored **locally on your device** only. The adhan
reminders are local notifications scheduled on your device; they do not transmit
any data.

---

## 2. Permissions we request and why

- **Location (fine/coarse):** to calculate accurate prayer times and the Qibla for
  your position. Optional — you can use a manually selected city instead.
- **Notifications:** to alert you (and play the adhan) at prayer times.
- **Exact alarms (schedule/use exact alarm):** so the adhan sounds at the exact
  time, even in battery-saver (Doze) mode.
- **Run at startup (boot completed):** to re-schedule prayer reminders after your
  device restarts.
- **Vibrate:** for notification vibration.

---

## 3. Third-party services

Salat relies on the following Google services, each governed by Google's own
privacy policy:

- **Google Firebase Analytics** — https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy
- **Google AdMob** — https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543
- **Google Privacy Policy** — https://policies.google.com/privacy

We do not share data with any other third parties.

---

## 4. Your choices and rights

- **Location:** grant, deny or revoke the permission in your device settings; use a
  manual city instead.
- **Ads personalization:** manage or reset your Advertising ID in
  *Android Settings → Privacy → Ads*, and adjust your consent choices.
- **Analytics:** you can limit ad/analytics tracking via your device's
  privacy/ads settings.
- Depending on your region (e.g. GDPR in the EEA/UK), you may have rights to
  access, correct or delete personal data. Since we do not hold personal data
  ourselves, such requests for analytics/ads data are handled by Google under their
  policies linked above. You may also contact us at the address below.

---

## 5. Children

Salat is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal
information from children. Ad content is configured to a family-friendly maximum
rating.

---

## 6. Data retention

We do not store your personal data. Locally cached data (your settings and last
known location) remains on your device until you clear the app's data or uninstall
the app. Analytics and advertising data are retained by Google according to their
retention policies.

---

## 7. Changes to this policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted at this
