## Appendix — Google Play "Data safety" form (developer notes, NOT part of the public policy)

When filling the Play Console **Data safety** section, declare what the app + its
SDKs (AdMob, Firebase Analytics) actually do. Suggested answers:

- **Does your app collect or share required user data?** Yes (via Google SDKs).
- **Data types — Location:** *Approximate location* and *Precise location* —
  **Collected** (used for app functionality; processed on-device, but the location
  permission is used). Mark **not shared** with you; note ads SDK may use coarse
  location. Purpose: App functionality (and Advertising, if AdMob uses it).
- **Device or other IDs:** **Collected / Shared** — by AdMob (Advertising ID) and
  Firebase. Purposes: Advertising/marketing, Analytics.
- **App activity / App interactions:** **Collected** — Firebase Analytics.
  Purpose: Analytics.
- **App info and performance (diagnostics/crash):** **Collected** — Firebase.
  Purpose: Analytics / app functionality.
- **Is data encrypted in transit?** Yes (Google SDKs use HTTPS).
- **Can users request deletion?** Provide the contact email; note most data is
  handled by Google.
- **Account / personal identifiers (name, email):** **Not collected** (no account).

